  "details": "# Issue:\n\nRight now the Notification Cell for Groups either only shows the Group Icon or the Picture of an Announcement, in both cases though it only says \"Group Notification\". This is not relay informative to the User and even the Verbose Mode Hud Popup shows more information.\n\n# Suggestion:  \n\nI have two ideas on how the information given in the Notification Cell could be improved:\n\n1. Since the space for Text is limited I would suggest to Show the Group Name and then what the Notification is about. Something like `VRCPrefabs: New Announcement` or `Community Meetup: Group Invention`. Obviously this can cause issues if the Group Name gets to long, in that case I would just end the name of the Group a bit early, e.g. `Communi... : Group Invention`.  \n\n2. Another option would be to just say what the Notification is about, e.g. `New Group Announcement` or `New Group Invention`, this would prevent issues with to long Group names.\n\n# Attachments:\n\nIn the picture below you can see how it currently looks:",
